Z||000008||mrfiero||10-25-2001||07:18 PM||||Sorry for the delay, but here is a picture of my 'original' Fiero ('88 GT) in front of the Fiero assembly plant in August 1995. <P>Sadly, this GT died a horrible death 4 months later (T-boned by a Nissan Maxima).  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackgt#2.JPG">  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroMontreal||10-25-2001||07:26 PM||||damn, nice pic!<P>Too bad the car is gone.. sigh..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> .. do you still have it for parts? Do you have any before and after pics?<BR>Thanx<BR>Alex||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||10-25-2001||08:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMontreal:<BR><B>damn, nice pic!<P>Too bad the car is gone.. sigh..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> .. do you still have it for parts? Do you have any before and after pics?<BR>Thanx<BR>Alex</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Believe me, I was bummed for a LONG time after the accident. In fact, I haven't been as attached to another Fiero since.  I owned that one for nearly 6 years and it was my only Fiero.....in the past 6 years since the wreck I have owned about 50 Fieros.....I just can't get comfortable with any of them.  I do have an identical '88 GT (minus the gold stripes) now.....it is my 'baby' with only 16K miles.  This one comes close to the original one, but I hate driving it since it has so few miles.<P>The engine in that GT was overhauled just a few days before that pic was taken.....I scrambled to get it done before the national show that year in Pontiac, MI.  At the time of the accident it had less than 6K miles on the new engine (113K overall).<P>It did get parted out....it took 6 months of screaming at the lady's insurance company before I got any $$, but it was worth the wait.  I got $6000 cash and got to keep the car!  I bought a T-Top '88 Formula with the $$ and swapped almost everything over (engine, tan leather interior, etc).<P>The only part I still have is the fastback panel and the only reason I still have it is it's a PITA to ship.   <P>I do have some 'after' pictures somewhere.  It doesn't look too bad in the pics, but the entire drivers side was screwed up.  Her car slid down the drivers side after hitting the left front wheel.....the left front wheel was pointing inward & the door was pushed in an inch (and bent the frame around the hinges).  The worst damage came at the end......when her car reached the left rear wheel it forced it back and actually ripped the engine cradle away from the frame!  The left rear wheel was pushed back into the rear fascia and was pointing outward.  It probably could drive itself in circles.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>At any rate, I'll try to dig up some pictures of the aftermath and will post them later.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroMontreal||10-25-2001||08:31 PM||||OMG :EEK: THATS A HORRIBLE DEATH! no fiero should die that way.. at least if you look on the bright side.. you are still alive.. were you injured in anyways?<P>Do you still have those 1/4 windows? PM me if you do.. I'd be interested..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfiero||10-25-2001||08:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMontreal:<BR><B>OMG :EEK: THATS A HORRIBLE DEATH! no fiero should die that way.. at least if you look on the bright side.. you are still alive.. were you injured in anyways?<P>Do you still have those 1/4 windows? PM me if you do.. I'd be interested..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  No injuries......just a messed up car.  I was driving at 40-45MPH and she was going 35-40MPH when we collided.  The Fiero is a very sturdy car.....the impact bar the runs the length of the door took the brunt of the impact and didn't protrude into the cabin area at all.  I had the window rolled down and it didn't even break!  That was pretty weird.<P>I only have the fastback panel left.....the quarter windows are long gone (I need a pair myself!).<P>Sorry.  <P>||||reg||1
