Z||000016||mrfiero||10-27-2001||06:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B> I took this pic of this display while at the Williamsburg show.<P>I don't remember the guy's name. He did tell it wasn't his car, but looked just like it.<P>Wish I had a better shot for you.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The burgundy Fiero is Tim Perrigo's (fieroparts.com).  The one in the pic is one he owned several years ago (had about 3300 miles).  It is identical to his 117 mile GT, so that is why he has it in the montage.<P>Tim probably has that pic (and one of mine as well) that is better than the one I posted.  He was with me at the plant in 1995 when the pic of my black car was taken.....his burgundy GT pic was taken at the same time.<P>I'll get ahold of Tim and will see if he can post a good picture of mine or his in front of the plant.    <P>||||reg||1
